    {
      "id": 25,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Safety and verification boundaries",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 68,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 5
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Primary training safety:** tagged synthetic records are rejected from live ingestion, stress records use their own database, and trainer/manual/JSON/export paths apply real-record filters. These are code/test guarantees to verify — there is no dataset-contamination gauge.\n\n**Evidence levels:** fixture/mock tests are reproducible without websites or API keys. A reachable service and a nonzero call counter do not prove a real website crawl or real external LLM call. Review actual receipts, source provenance and dated verification results before claiming a complete live pipeline.\n\n**Not exported:** broker/JMX health, whole consumer-group lag, per-origin Processor writes, result-Processor completion totals, labelled extraction accuracy, confidence calibration or external API cost. Do not infer them from these panels."
      }
